{% extends "layouts/admin.njk" %}

{% block title %}Vocabulary — Admin{% endblock %}

{#
  What each relationship type is allowed to connect.

  Migration 0014 seeded a value for every predicate it found. Those values are
  a judgement about a history vocabulary rather than a fact about the schema,
  and a refusal is hard, so they have to be correctable here: a domain that is
  too narrow would block a claim the sources support, and fixing it must not
  need a second migration.

  Unchecking every box on a side stores "no opinion", not "connects nothing" --
  a verb that connects nothing could never be used. Retiring a verb is deleting
  it, which this screen deliberately does not do: `relationship.predicate_id`
  is a RESTRICT foreign key, so a verb in use cannot be removed without first
  deciding what happens to every edge asserted with it.

  Every label here is operator-supplied text under autoescape. Nothing is
  marked safe.
#}
{% block content %}
  <h1>Vocabulary</h1>

  <p class="hint">
    Each relationship type may be limited to the kinds of item it makes sense
    between — “Born in” joins a person to a place. A type with nothing ticked
    on a side accepts any kind there, which is what every type did before this
    screen existed.
  </p>
  <p class="hint">
    Changing a type governs what may be asserted from now on. Connections
    already recorded are never re-checked and never removed.
  </p>

  <ul class="vocabulary-list">
    {% for predicate in predicates %}
      <li>
        <form method="post" action="/admin/vocabulary/{{ predicate.id }}" class="vocabulary-form">
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrfToken }}" />

          <h2>{{ predicate.label }}</h2>
          <p class="muted small">
            Read the other way: {{ predicate.inverseLabel }}
            {% if predicate.isSymmetric %} · says the same thing both ways{% endif %}
            · <code>{{ predicate.code }}</code>
          </p>

          <fieldset>
            <legend>From</legend>
            {% for kind in kinds %}
              <label class="checkbox">
                <input type="checkbox" name="domainKinds" value="{{ kind }}"
                       {% if predicate.domainKinds and kind in predicate.domainKinds %}checked{% endif %} />
                {{ kind }}
              </label>
            {% endfor %}
          </fieldset>

          <fieldset>
            <legend>To</legend>
            {% for kind in kinds %}
              <label class="checkbox">
                <input type="checkbox" name="rangeKinds" value="{{ kind }}"
                       {% if predicate.rangeKinds and kind in predicate.rangeKinds %}checked{% endif %} />
                {{ kind }}
              </label>
            {% endfor %}
          </fieldset>

          <button type="submit">Save</button>
        </form>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% endblock %}
